    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Italian eggplant is a specific variety of eggplant known for being slightly smaller, shorter, and plumper than the standard American globe eggplant, featuring a tear-drop shape and a more delicate, sweeter flavor profile. It has a deep purple, glossy skin and tender flesh that acts like a sponge, making it highly prized in Mediterranean cuisine.</span></p>",
